{"timestamp":"2026-09-14T10:37:35.214Z","ordinal":501,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a09f7e-626e-7230-a636-b4888ee311e9","call_id":"call_aYSXdhSQo1u79kW5oe2jJjNV","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n===== houdini-style =====\n  leve une `PermissionError` qui ne nomme rien. Seule la largeur s ecrit, la hauteur suit.\n- `hou.hmath.buildLookatRotation` n existe pas, le nom juste est `buildRotateLookAt`.\n- `distantlight::3.0` n existe pas sur Houdini 22.0.368, seul `distantlight::2.0` est la.\n- Sans `partitionattribs = name` sur `sopimport`, toute l eglise arrive en un seul `mesh_0` : un seul\n  prim, donc un seul materiau possible pour 15 585 primitives.\n\n### Style Shorts Houdini, Titre Inter Tight et Typographie Randomisee par Mot (2026-09-13)\n\nPour les shorts de presentation de textures, procedurals ou composants Houdini :\n- **Format** : Vertical 2160x3840 (4K) a 60 fps (H.264/AAC, master mov avc1 et mp4, bitrate video eleve crf 17). Jamais de sortie HD.\n- **Structure (18.00s exact)** :\n  1. Sequence turntable Karma XPU en plancher d accroche (secondes 0 a 3).\n  2. Sequence walkthrough procedural ecran entier Layout 2 (secondes 3 a 15).\n  3. Defile de validation 3 spheres de vitrine crops 1:1 sans deplacement (secondes 15 a 18 : Cathedral Grain, Wood Knot, Composite Blend).\n- **Titre Superieur Flottant Sans Capsule** :\n  - Texte : « Houdini Procedural Texturing »\n  - Titre epure direct flottant : zero capsule, aucun fond ni bordure sombre. Le texte repose directement au-dessus de la vue avec contour noir de decoupe.\n  - Triptyque typographique en italique pur :\n    * « Houdini » : `Canela-BoldItalic-Cy-Gr-Web.ttf` (taille 132 pt en 4K), terminaisons evasees nobles et pleins contrastes\n    * « Procedural » : `InterTight-Italic-VariableFont_wght.ttf` (axe 700, taille 132 pt en 4K), assise centrale moderne et puissante\n    * « Texturing » : `AnthropicMono-Bold.ttf` avec inclinaison oblique a 12 degres (taille 132 pt en 4K), touche technique en harmonie d inclinaison\n  - Couleur : blanc pur `#FFFFFF` avec contour de decoupe noir (`stroke_width=8` en 4K, `stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0)`)\n  - Alignement : verrouillage rigoureux sur la meme baseline (`anchor=\"ls\"`)\n- **Sous-Titres (Subtitles)** :\n  - Trio typographique valide avec alternance dynamique par mot (sans repetition consecutive) :\n    1. Inter Tight Bold Italic (`InterTight-Italic-VariableFont_wght.ttf`, 700, 96 pt en 4K)\n    2. Anthropic Serif SemiBold Italic (`AnthropicSerif-SemiBoldItalic.ttf`, 96 pt en 4K)\n    3. Anthropic Mono Bold Italic (`AnthropicMono-Bold.ttf`, transformation oblique 12 degres identique au titre, 88 pt en 4K)\n  - Harmonie complete d inclinaison : cent pour cent des mots du titre et des sous-titres partagent l inclinaison a 12 degres\n  - Couleur : jaune vif plein `#FFE144`\n  - Contour noir : `stroke_width=8` en 4K, `stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0)`\n  - Alignement strict sur la baseline : verrouillage par `anchor=\"ls\"`, supprimant tout decalage ou saut vertical entre mots de polices differentes\n  - Positionnement vertical en 4K : Y baseline de depart = 3040 px, interligne = 152 px, espacement horizontal = 32 px\n\n### Audio et Musique de Fond via yt-dlp (Pipeline 18s)\n\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n===== canela-context =====\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-5-## 1. La formule tri-font ZenRay\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-6-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-7-Le titrage epure de ZenRay repose sur l association de trois polices complementaires :\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md:8:1. **Mot 1 (Marque / Outil) : Canela Bold Italic** (corps 66 pt). Apporte l elegance classique et la personnalite editee.\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-9-2. **Mot 2 (Methode) : Inter Tight Italic** (corps 66 pt, variable font wght 700). Offre la precision technique et la modernite suisse.\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-10-3. **Mot 3 (Discipline) : Anthropic Mono Bold simulee en italique** (corps 66 pt, affine shear 0.22). Apporte le cote developpeur et codeur rigoureux.\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-11-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md:12:Exemple applique au Short : `Houdini` (Canela) + `Procedural` (Inter Tight) + `Texturing` (Mono Italic slante).\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-13-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-14-## 2. Prevention de collision de variables (Le piege w1 / w2)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-15-\n--\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-25-d_title = ImageDraw.Draw(title_layer)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-26-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-27-# Rendu complet du titre une seule fois au boot\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md:28:d_title.text((title_tx, title_baseline_y), 'Houdini', font=title_canela, fill=(255, 255, 255), stroke_width=4, stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0), anchor='ls')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-29-d_title.text((title_tx + t_w1 + space_w, title_baseline_y), 'Procedural', font=title_inter, fill=(255, 255, 255), stroke_width=4, stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0), anchor='ls')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-30-title_layer.paste(slanted_title_mono, paste_title_mono_pos, slanted_title_mono)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/05-typography-and-title-rules.md-31-\n--\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-19-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-20-1. **Secondes 0,0 a 3,0 (Accroche Hero / Lookdev) :**\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-21-   - Rendu en direct de l asset (Karma XPU sous Solaris) ou turntable 3D eclairée.\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md:22:   - Titre epure sans capsule sombre, compose de trois polices harmonisees (Canela Bold Italic, Inter Tight Italic et Anthropic Mono Bold simulee en italique).\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-23-   - Declenchement du premier cue de sous-titres.\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-24-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/SKILL.md-25-2. **Secondes 3,0 a 15,0 (Workflow procedural / Graphe Houdini) :**\n--\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-7-TOTAL_FRAMES = 18 * FPS # 1080 frames = 18.00s exact\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-8-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-9-font_dir = os.path.expanduser('~/Library/Fonts')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py:10:p_canela = os.path.join(font_dir, 'Canela-BoldItalic-Cy-Gr-Web.ttf')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-11-p_inter = os.path.join(font_dir, 'InterTight-Italic-VariableFont_wght.ttf')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-12-p_serif = os.path.join(font_dir, 'AnthropicSerif-SemiBoldItalic.ttf')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-13-p_mono = os.path.join(font_dir, 'AnthropicMono-Bold.ttf')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-14-p_sans = os.path.join(font_dir, 'AnthropicSans-Bold.ttf')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-15-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-16-# 1. Master Title setup (PRE-RENDERED ONCE TO AVOID ANY VARIABLE SHADOWING)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py:17:title_canela = ImageFont.truetype(p_canela, 66)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-18-title_inter = ImageFont.truetype(p_inter, 66)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-19-title_inter.set_variation_by_axes([700])\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-20-title_mono = ImageFont.truetype(p_mono, 66)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-21-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py:22:t_w1 = title_canela.getlength('Houdini')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-23-space_w = 18\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-24-t_w2 = title_inter.getlength('Procedural')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-25-t_w3 = title_mono.getlength('Texturing')\n--\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-41-\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-42-title_layer = Image.new('RGBA', (W, H), (0, 0, 0, 0))\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-43-t_draw = ImageDraw.Draw(title_layer)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py:44:t_draw.text((title_tx, title_baseline_y), 'Houdini', font=title_canela, fill=(255, 255, 255), stroke_width=4, stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0), anchor='ls')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-45-t_draw.text((title_tx + t_w1 + space_w, title_baseline_y), 'Procedural', font=title_inter, fill=(255, 255, 255), stroke_width=4, stroke_fill=(0, 0, 0), anchor='ls')\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-46-title_layer.paste(slanted_title_mono, paste_title_mono_pos, slanted_title_mono)\n/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-realisation-shorts-reels/components/02-python-compositor-script.py-47-\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n===== current-render =====\n\"\"\"Render the animated subtitle and title overlay for a 30 second short, piped straight into ffmpeg.\n\nWHY A PIPE. 900 RGBA frames at 2160x3840 would mean writing and re-reading about 28 GB of PNGs. Streaming\nraw frames to ffmpeg's stdin, as a second input, skips that entirely: no intermediate files, no\ncompression overhead, one process reads what the other writes.\n\nFR : le pipe evite d ecrire puis relire des gigaoctets de PNG intermediaires.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\n\n# -- PARAMETERS (HDA law: everything tunable lives here) -----------------------------------------\nP = {\n    'width': 2160,\n    'height': 3840,\n    'fps': 30,\n    'duration': 30.0,\n    # Corrected 2026-09-12, final pass: the title is MIXED. \"Houdini\" keeps sentence case (not\n    # HOUDINI) in AnthropicSerif SemiBold, upright. The rest, \"LOUISIANA BAYOU\", stays uppercase\n    # in AnthropicSerif SemiBold ITALIC. Matthieu: \"c'etait Houdini pas en caps ... pas italic\n    # mais le reste du titre est italic\".\n    # FR : \"Houdini\" en casse normale et droit, \"LOUISIANA BAYOU\" en majuscules et italique.\n    'title_font': '/Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSerif-SemiBold.ttf',\n    'title_font_italic': '/Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSerif-SemiBoldItalic.ttf',\n    # Corrected again: NO forced uppercase anywhere in the title, sentence case throughout.\n    # Matthieu: \"NON TOUT EN CASSE NORMAL\".\n    # FR : plus aucune majuscule forcee, casse normale partout.\n    'title_text_upright': 'Houdini',\n    'title_text_italic': ' Louisiana Bayou',\n    'title_size_start': 260,           # the title is sized to the MAXIMUM px that still fits, never cropped\n    'title_max_pill_width_ratio': 0.92,\n    'title_pill_bg': (255, 255, 255, 255),\n    'title_text_color': (0, 0, 0, 255),\n    'title_radius_ratio': 0.30,\n    'title_pad_x_ratio': 0.55,\n    'title_pad_y_ratio': 0.42,\n    'title_y_center': 520,\n    'subtitle_font': '/Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/InterVariable.ttf',\n    # Corrected 2026-09-12: the bottom subtitles are Inter ExtraBold (800), not SemiBold (600).\n    # FR : les sous-titres du bas sont en Inter ExtraBold, pas SemiBold.\n    # Corrected 2026-09-12, final pass: #f8f671 read as too washed out. Matthieu: \"un jaune\n    # complet normal\". Pure vivid yellow, the same #FFE600 already documented as \"jaune vif\" in\n    # this skill's own history (section 6), not a pale tint.\n    # FR : jaune vif plein, pas une teinte pale.\n    'subtitle_weight': 900,\n    'subtitle_color': (0xFF, 0xE6, 0x00, 255),\n    'subtitle_size_start': 124,\n    'subtitle_max_width_ratio': 0.86,\n    'line1_y': 3040,\n    'line2_y': 3220,\n    'cue_seconds': 3.0,\n    'pop_line1_offset': 0.0,\n    'pop_line2_offset': 0.4,\n    # (time, scale, opacity) keyframes of the pop-in envelope, held at the last value after.\n    'pop_keys': [(0.0, 0.5, 0.0), (0.05, 0.5, 1.0), (0.15, 1.18, 1.0), (0.30, 0.96, 1.0), (0.45, 1.0, 1.0)],\n}\n\nCUES = [\n    (\"Today I continued developing\", \"my procedural Louisiana bayou church in Houdini.\"),\n    (\"I added a new asymmetrical vestibule\", \"on the porch stairs.\"),\n    (\"It sits off-center\", \"as part of the porch entrance.\"),\n    (\"I also started a Copernicus workflow\", \"for procedural materials like Substance Designer.\"),\n    (\"Its advantage is staying\", \"inside the same software.\"),\n    (\"I will see how far Copernicus can go\", \"compared with Substance Designer.\"),\n    (\"Across my existing components,\", \"I identified the material tags.\"),\n    (\"Those tags assign materials\", \"directly to the geometry.\"),\n    (\"I chose four materials from\", \"my concept art and reference images.\"),\n    (\"Next is the Karma XPU lookdev render.\", \"The complete graph is already set up.\"),\n]\n\n\nWEIGHT_NAMES = {400: b'Regular', 500: b'Medium', 600: b'SemiBold', 700: b'Bold',\n                800: b'ExtraBold', 900: b'Black'}\n\n\ndef load_variable_font(path, size, weight):\n    # InterVariable carries TWO axes, optical size then weight: set_variation_by_axes([weight])\n    # silently sets the FIRST axis (optical size) instead, and the glyphs stay Regular.\n    # The named instance is unambiguous and matches exactly what \"ExtraBold\" means.\n    # FR : passer un seul poids regle le premier axe (optical size), pas le poids ; le nom evite l erreur.\n    font = ImageFont.truetype(path, size)\n    try:\n        font.set_variation_by_name(WEIGHT_NAMES.get(weight, b'Regular'))\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return font\n\n\ndef fit_font(text, path, start_size, max_width, weight=None):\n    size = start_size\n    while size > 20:\n        font = (load_variable_font(path, size, weight) if weight else ImageFont.truetype(path, size))\n        box = font.getbbox(text)\n        if (box[2] - box[0]) <= max_width:\n            return font, box\n        size -= 2\n    font = (load_variable_font(path, size, weight) if weight else ImageFont.truetype(path, size))\n    return font, font.getbbox(text)\n\n\ndef make_text_sprite(text, font, color, pad=12):\n    \"\"\"A tight RGBA sprite, so scaling it later scales the glyphs around their own center.\"\"\"\n    box = font.getbbox(text)\n    width = box[2] - box[0] + pad * 2\n    height = box[3] - box[1] + pad * 2\n    sprite = Image.new('RGBA', (width, height), (0, 0, 0, 0))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(sprite)\n    draw.text((pad - box[0], pad - box[1]), text, font=font, fill=color)\n    return sprite\n\n\ndef build_title_layer():\n    \"\"\"Two runs, two fonts, one baseline. \"Houdini\" is upright, the rest is italic: PIL has no\n    mixed-style text drawing, so the title is measured and placed as two separate runs that share\n    the SAME baseline, computed from each font's own ascent, not from the bounding box top.\"\"\"\n    # Grow the title to the largest size whose PILL still fits inside the canvas with a margin:\n    # the size is not guessed, it is measured against the real pill width at each step.\n    # FR : la taille se mesure contre la vraie largeur de pastille, jamais devinee.\n    max_pill_width = int(P['width'] * P['title_max_pill_width_ratio'])\n    size = P['title_size_start']\n    while size > 24:\n        font_up = ImageFont.truetype(P['title_font'], size)\n        font_it = ImageFont.truetype(P['title_font_italic'], size)\n        w_up = font_up.getlength(P['title_text_upright'])\n        w_it = font_it.getlength(P['title_text_italic'])\n        ascent_up, descent_up = font_up.getmetrics()\n        ascent_it, descent_it = font_it.getmetrics()\n        cap_h = max(ascent_up, ascent_it)          # used only to size the padding, as before\n        pad_x = int(cap_h * P['title_pad_x_ratio'])\n        pill_w = w_up + w_it + pad_x * 2\n        if pill_w <= max_pill_width:\n            break\n        size -= 2\n\n    ascent = max(ascent_up, ascent_it)\n    descent = max(descent_up, descent_it)\n    text_h = ascent + descent\n    pad_x = int(cap_h * P['title_pad_x_ratio'])\n    pad_y = int(cap_h * P['title_pad_y_ratio'])\n    text_w = w_up + w_it\n    pill_w, pill_h = text_w + pad_x * 2, text_h + pad_y * 2\n    radius = int(pill_h * P['title_radius_ratio'])\n\n    layer = Image.new('RGBA', (P['width'], P['height']), (0, 0, 0, 0))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(layer)\n    x0 = (P['width'] - pill_w) // 2\n    y0 = P['title_y_center'] - pill_h // 2\n    draw.rounded_rectangle([x0, y0, x0 + pill_w, y0 + pill_h], radius=radius, fill=P['title_pill_bg'])\n\n    baseline_y = y0 + pad_y + ascent\n    draw.text((x0 + pad_x, baseline_y - ascent_up), P['title_text_upright'], font=font_up,\n              fill=P['title_text_color'])\n    draw.text((x0 + pad_x + w_up, baseline_y - ascent_it), P['title_text_italic'], font=font_it,\n              fill=P['title_text_color'])\n    return layer\n\n\ndef envelope(local_t):\n    keys = P['pop_keys']\n    if local_t <= keys[0][0]:\n        return keys[0][1], keys[0][2]\n    if local_t >= keys[-1][0]:\n        return keys[-1][1], keys[-1][2]\n    for (t0, s0, o0), (t1, s1, o1) in zip(keys, keys[1:]):\n        if t0 <= local_t <= t1:\n            f = (local_t - t0) / (t1 - t0)\n            return s0 + (s1 - s0) * f, o0 + (o1 - o0) * f\n    return keys[-1][1], keys[-1][2]\n\n\ndef paste_scaled(base, sprite, center_x, center_y, scale, opacity):\n    if opacity <= 0.0 or scale <= 0.0:\n        return\n    w, h = sprite.size\n    new_w, new_h = max(1, int(w * scale)), max(1, int(h * scale))\n    resized = sprite.resize((new_w, new_h), Image.LANCZOS)\n    if opacity < 1.0:\n        alpha = resized.getchannel('A').point(lambda a: int(a * opacity))\n        resized.putalpha(alpha)\n    base.alpha_composite(resized, (int(center_x - new_w / 2), int(center_y - new_h / 2)))\n\n\ndef main():\n    max_width = int(P['width'] * P['subtitle_max_width_ratio'])\n    sprites = []\n    for line1, line2 in CUES:\n        font1, _ = fit_font(line1, P['subtitle_font'], P['subtitle_size_start'], max_width, P['subtitle_weight'])\n        font2, _ = fit_font(line2, P['subtitle_font'], P['subtitle_size_start'], max_width, P['subtitle_weight'])\n        sprites.append((make_text_sprite(line1, font1, P['subtitle_color']),\n                        make_text_sprite(line2, font2, P['subtitle_color'])))\n\n    title_layer = build_title_layer()\n\n    total_frames = int(round(P['duration'] * P['fps']))\n    out = sys.stdout.buffer\n    for frame_index in range(total_frames):\n        t = frame_index / P['fps']\n        cue_index = min(int(t // P['cue_seconds']), len(CUES) - 1)\n        local_t = t - cue_index * P['cue_seconds']\n        sprite1, sprite2 = sprites[cue_index]\n\n        frame = title_layer.copy()\n        scale1, opacity1 = envelope(max(0.0, local_t - P['pop_line1_offset']))\n        scale2, opacity2 = envelope(max(0.0, local_t - P['pop_line2_offset']))\n        if local_t < P['pop_line2_offset']:\n            opacity2 = 0.0\n        paste_scaled(frame, sprite1, P['width'] / 2, P['line1_y'], scale1, opacity1)\n        paste_scaled(frame, sprite2, P['width'] / 2, P['line2_y'], scale2, opacity2)\n\n        out.write(frame.tobytes())\n    out.flush()\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Updated 2026-09-14 00:25 CEST: 4K is the only output resolution.\n    main()\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n===== font-